def("u4l4", "Peloton Workout Alerts", ["**You are on the Peloton software team.** During a class the bike screen watches the rider's numbers and pops up messages. An **if** statement runs its indented lines only when its condition is True."],
  ["if statements", "indentation decides what belongs to the if", "conditions with and", "an if that changes a variable", "several ifs in a row", "an if inside an if"], [
  S("A first alert", ["Ask `Heart rate? ` as a whole number in **`heart_rate`**. **If** the heart rate is **over `170`**, print `Slow down`."],
    "Ask and add the alert.", `heart_rate = int(input("Heart rate? "))\nif heart_rate > 170:\n    print("Slow down")`,
    [["heart_rate from input as a whole number", /^\s*heart_rate\s*=\s*int\(\s*input\(/m], ["an if on heart_rate over 170", /^\s*if\s+heart_rate\s*>\s*170\s*:/m]],
    "Run it and type 180.", [["Slow down", /Slow down/]]),
  S("What belongs to the if", ["A second alert line, `Drink water`, must show up **only** when the alert fires, so it belongs inside the same if. Then print `Workout saved` so that it shows **every time**, whether or not the alert fired."],
    "Edit your program: add the second alert and the saved line.", "", [["Drink water inside the if", /^\s+print\(\s*["']Drink water["']\s*\)/m], ["Workout saved outside the if", /^print\(\s*["']Workout saved["']\s*\)/m]],
    "Run it with 180, then run it with 120 and watch the difference.", [["Drink water", /Drink water/], ["Workout saved", /Workout saved/]],
    `heart_rate = int(input("Heart rate? "))\nif heart_rate > 170:\n    print("Slow down")\n    print("Drink water")\nprint("Workout saved")`),
  S("Conditions with logic", ["Make **`has_monitor`** equal to `True`. Add an **if** that prints `Red zone` only when the rider has a monitor **and** the heart rate is at least `150`."],
    "Add the variable and the if.", `has_monitor = True\nif has_monitor and heart_rate >= 150:\n    print("Red zone")`,
    [["has_monitor is True", V("has_monitor", "True")], ["an if combining has_monitor and the heart rate", /^\s*if\s+has_monitor\s+and\s+heart_rate\s*>=\s*150\s*:/m]],
    "Run it with 180.", [["Red zone", /Red zone/]]),
  S("An if that changes a variable", ["Riders earn points. Make **`points`** equal to `40`. **If** the heart rate is at least `160`, add `10` to the points. After the if, print `Points:` followed by the points."],
    "Add the points and the if.", `points = 40\nif heart_rate >= 160:\n    points = points + 10\nprint("Points:", points)`,
    [["points is 40", V("points", "40")], ["an if on heart_rate at least 160", /^\s*if\s+heart_rate\s*>=\s*160\s*:/m], ["points go up by 10 inside the if", /^\s+points\s*(=\s*points\s*\+\s*10|\+=\s*10)/m]],
    "Run it with 180.", [["Points: 50", /Points: 50/]]),
  S("Separate ifs and a nested if", ["Make **`cadence`** equal to `85`. Use **two separate ifs** (not an elif): one prints `Fast pedaling` when the cadence is over `80` and the other prints `Good pedaling` when it is over `60`, so a cadence of 85 prints both. Then use an **if inside an if**: when the heart rate is over `100` **and then, inside that**, the cadence is over `80`, print `Peak interval`."],
    "Add the three ifs.", `cadence = 85\nif cadence > 80:\n    print("Fast pedaling")\nif cadence > 60:\n    print("Good pedaling")\nif heart_rate > 100:\n    if cadence > 80:\n        print("Peak interval")`,
    [["cadence is 85", V("cadence", "85")], ["an if for cadence over 80", /^\s*if\s+cadence\s*>\s*80\s*:/m], ["a separate if for cadence over 60", /^\s*if\s+cadence\s*>\s*60\s*:/m], ["an if inside an if", /^\s+if\s+cadence\s*>\s*80\s*:/m]],
    "Run it with 180.", [["Fast pedaling", /Fast pedaling/], ["Good pedaling", /Good pedaling/], ["Peak interval", /Peak interval/]])],
  [{ answers: [["Heart", "180"]] }]);

